Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.25,0:00:02.38,Default,,0,0,0,,August again. The\NDembi Dollo rain hasn't
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.38,0:00:04.68,Default,,0,0,0,,changed—but your voice,\Nthe one that warmed this
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.68,0:00:05.68,Default,,0,0,0,,house, is gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.25,0:00:11.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Your guitar still rests where\Nyou left it. With just six
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.25,0:00:14.09,Default,,0,0,0,,strings, you wrote songs\Nthat fought for your people.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.25,0:00:19.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You weren't only a singer.\NYou taught children Qubee,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.51,0:00:22.21,Default,,0,0,0,,so they could finally\Nwrite their own names.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.25,0:00:26.30,Default,,0,0,0,,People listened to your\Ncassettes in secret. I kept
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.30,0:00:28.74,Default,,0,0,0,,your old tape and\Nnotebook of poems safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.25,0:00:34.45,Default,,0,0,0,,You wrote these words in\Nblue ink. Before leaving for
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.45,0:00:36.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Finfinnee, you sang to me:\N'Mother of a hero, do not
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.95,0:00:37.95,Default,,0,0,0,,weep.'
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.25,0:00:42.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Then in August ninety-six,\Na bullet in Finfinnee
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.51,0:00:45.81,Default,,0,0,0,,silenced you. Since that\Nnight, this house has lived
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.81,0:00:46.81,Default,,0,0,0,,in silence.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.25,0:00:51.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Tonight, I refuse the\Nsilence. I am not a singer,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.27,0:00:53.72,Default,,0,0,0,,my son—only a mother\Nwho misses you. I will try
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.72,0:00:54.72,Default,,0,0,0,,one note.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.25,0:00:59.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I pluck one worn\Nstring. They killed the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.66,0:01:01.59,Default,,0,0,0,,singer—never the song.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.25,0:01:04.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen, my son. Beyond\Nmy doorway, a new
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.73,0:01:07.55,Default,,0,0,0,,generation—not even born\Nback then—knows every
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.55,0:01:08.55,Default,,0,0,0,,word you wrote.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.25,0:01:13.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Look—through the rain,\Nthey are singing your voice
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.31,0:01:16.55,Default,,0,0,0,,back to you. And tonight,\Nmy son... I am not weeping.
